  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\text{u}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $\\text{v}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we construct a matrix where the columns are made up of the components of the corresponding vectors:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we find the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(M) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{3}{2})\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =3-3 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe absolute value of $det(M)$ gives the area $A$ of the parallelogram:\n\n$$\nA=|\\,0\\,|=0\n$$",
